{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794862138021,"sessionID":"ses_e19e37d77ffeBadt3udLmrManh","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_01a1e61c91c775e2b7c21004","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Trace import report failure","prompt":"Explore this repository thoroughly enough to diagnose the reported March Rabobank CSV import/income-report bug. Do not modify files. Locate and report: (1) the Rabo CSV import implementation and how rows become transactions; (2) transaction amount/currency parsing and any None values; (3) FX conversion and home-currency selection; (4) income report aggregation; (5) existing tests and fixtures for Rabo imports, imports, FX, and income reports; (6) documented test/lint/typecheck commands in README or project config. Inspect the likely causal path, including how a 'Saldo begin' row might be handled, and suggest the smallest robust fix satisfying atomic import semantics (if a statement line cannot be read, name file and line, add nothing). Return exact file paths and relevant line numbers plus test locations. Thoroughness: very thorough.","subagent_type":"explore","command":"Investigate the reported March Rabobank import and income-report TypeError"},"output":"<task id=\"ses_e19e36aaeffejQt8DEUBzCH6km\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\n## Diagnosis\n\nThe March failure is **not caused by missing EUR exchange rates**. There are two related defects in the Rabobank reader:\n\n1. The Dutch amount grammar rejects a leading `+`, even though the documented Rabo format and the reported statement use it.\n2. When a Rabo amount cannot be parsed, the reader does not consistently reject the row; it creates a transaction whose `amount` is `None`.\n\nThe second defect violates the README’s atomic-import promise and defers the error until the income report tries to multiply `None` by the EUR conversion rate.\n\nNo files were modified; the working tree remains clean.\n\n---\n\n# 1. Rabobank CSV import and transaction creation\n\n## CLI entry point\n\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/__main__.py:56-59`\n  - Defines `import FILE --format generic|ing|rabo --account ID`.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/__main__.py:102-109`\n  - Calls `import_statement(...)`.\n  - Prints the `ImportResult` summary and currency warnings.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/__main__.py:148-149`\n  - Saves the ledger only after the import command completes successfully.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/__main__.py:153-159`\n  - Catches `LedgerError`, prints `error: ...`, and exits with status 2.\n  - `ImportError_` is a `LedgerError`, so a correctly raised import error would produce a friendly message rather than a traceback.\n\n## CSV row handling\n\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/io/csv_import.py:46-57`\n  - `csv.DictReader` parses the CSV.\n  - Empty files are rejected at lines 48-49.\n  - Rows with too many fields are rejected with the physical file line at lines 51-54.\n  - Completely blank rows are skipped at lines 55-56.\n  - Each yielded row carries `reader.line_num`, i.e. the physical CSV line number, and normalized header keys at line 57.\n\n## Reader dispatch and staging\n\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/io/csv_import.py:60-70`\n  - Validates the format, reads the bytes, enforces the size limit, and decodes the file.\n  - Line 70 materializes the entire reader result with `list(...)`.\n  - That `list(...)` is important for atomicity: if any row raises during parsing, `read_statement()` never returns and `import_statement()` never reaches `journal.extend()`.\n\n## Import orchestration\n\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/io/csv_import.py:73-93`\n  - Line 76 explicitly promises “all of them, or none on an error.”\n  - Line 79 reads and parses the complete file before changing the journal.\n  - Lines 81-85 warn when statement currencies differ from the account currency.\n  - Lines 86-91 categorize the parsed transactions.\n  - Line 92 adds them to the journal.\n\nThus, a parse exception raised by a reader is already atomic with respect to journal entries: even if valid rows precede the bad row, `journal.extend()` has not yet been called.\n\n## Rabobank reader\n\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py:11-13`\n  - Documents signed Rabo amounts, including `+1.250,00`.\n  - Documents that `Saldo ...` rows carry no amount and are skipped.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py:108-110`\n  - `_is_balance_line()` checks whether stripped, lowercased `Omschrijving-1` starts with `saldo`.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py:112-126`\n  - Line 114 parses `Bedrag`.\n  - Lines 115-116 skip an amountless balance row.\n  - Lines 117-126 create the `Transaction`.\n  - Line 120 assigns `amount=amount` with `# type: ignore[arg-type]`, masking the fact that `amount` can still be `None` at that point.\n  - Line 121 reads `Munt`, defaulting to EUR and uppercasing it.\n  - Line 125 records the source as `<file>:<line>`.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py:129-130`\n  - Maps `rabo` to `read_rabo` and comma delimiter.\n\n## How `Saldo begin` is handled\n\nFor the reported row:\n\n```csv\n2026-03-01,,EUR,,,Saldo begin\n```\n\nthe path is:\n\n1. `Bedrag` is empty.\n2. `parse_amount()` returns `None`.\n3. `_is_balance_line()` sees `Saldo begin` and returns true.\n4. `read_rabo()` executes `continue`.\n5. No transaction is created.\n\nThat is correct and is why the reported import says `3 read`, not `4 read`: the balance row is skipped and the other three rows are counted.\n\nThere is one related edge case: because the current condition is `amount is None and _is_balance_line(row)`, a `Saldo` row with a nonempty amount would be treated as a transaction. This is not the reported failure, but moving the balance-line check ahead of amount validation would more faithfully implement the documented “balance lines are skipped” rule.\n\n---\n\n# 2. Amount/currency parsing and `None` propagation\n\n## Amount parser\n\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py:30-51`\n  - Line 31 defines the Dutch-number grammar:\n\n    ```python\n    EURO_AMOUNT = re.compile(r\"^-?(\\d{1,3}(\\.\\d{3})+|\\d+),\\d{2}$\")\n    ```\n\n    It accepts an optional minus sign but **not** an optional plus sign.\n  - Lines 40-42 return `None` for an empty/whitespace cell.\n  - Lines 43-46 reject any decimal-comma value that does not match `EURO_AMOUNT`.\n  - Lines 47-51 are the decimal-point path; `Decimal` accepts a leading plus there.\n\nTherefore:\n\n```text\nparse_amount(\"+2.750,00\", decimal_comma=True) -> None\nparse_amount(\"-1.020,00\", decimal_comma=True) -> Decimal(\"-1020.00\")\n```\n\nThe generic parser accepts a leading plus because it uses `Decimal` directly, but the Rabo parser does not.\n\n## Readers differ in how they handle `None`\n\n- Generic reader:\n  - `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py:67-81`\n  - Lines 69-71 raise `ImportError_` if the amount is `None`.\n- ING reader:\n  - `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py:84-105`\n  - Lines 86-90 do the same.\n- Rabo reader:\n  - `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py:114-120`\n  - It skips `None` only for a recognized balance line.\n  - For every other `None`, it yields a `Transaction` with `amount=None`.\n\nThat Rabo branch is the malformed-input hole.\n\n## Why the invalid row is accepted during import\n\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/core/transactions.py:11-26`\n  - `Transaction.amount` is annotated as `Decimal`, but there is no runtime validation.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/core/transactions.py:28-42`\n  - The fingerprint merely uses `str(self.amount)`, so the invalid row gets a fingerprint based on the text `\"None\"`.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/core/transactions.py:54-75`\n  - `to_dict()` explicitly serializes `None` as JSON null.\n  - `from_dict()` explicitly accepts null and reconstructs `amount=None`.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/core/journal.py:27-41`\n  - `Journal.add()` checks the account and category but does not validate the amount.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/rules/categorize.py:39-44,80-85`\n  - Rule matching uses `(transaction.amount or 0)`.\n  - A `None` amount therefore looks like zero during categorization.\n  - The invalid salary becomes `uncategorised` rather than `salary`.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/rules/matchers.py:63-72`\n  - Amount matchers also explicitly tolerate `None`.\n\nThese fallbacks let the bad transaction pass through import without an error. They do not make it valid; they merely postpone the failure.\n\n## Currency parsing\n\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py:121`\n  - Rabo currency is `(Munt or \"EUR\").strip().upper()`.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py:76`\n  - Generic currency uses the same normalization.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py:100`\n  - ING is fixed to EUR.\n\nNo Rabo currency validation occurs during import. Unknown currencies are only encountered by the FX layer later. That is a separate robustness gap, not the cause here.\n\n---\n\n# 3. FX conversion and home-currency selection\n\n## Conversion path\n\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/fx/convert.py:12-16`\n  - `to_home()` looks up a rate and executes:\n\n    ```python\n    return round_cents(amount * rate)\n    ```\n\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/fx/convert.py:19-21`\n  - `transaction_in_home()` passes `transaction.amount` directly into `to_home()`.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/fx/convert.py:24-25`\n  - `convert_all()` converts every transaction, including EUR transactions.\n\nThere is no guard for `None` here. With an invalid salary, the failing operation is effectively:\n\n```text\nNone * Decimal(\"1\")\n```\n\nwhich raises:\n\n```text\nTypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for *: 'NoneType' and 'decimal.Decimal'\n```\n\n## Why EUR still goes through “conversion”\n\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/core/money.py:8-10`\n  - The default home currency is EUR.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/fx/rates.py:23-25`\n  - `RateTable.home` defaults to that home currency and is validated.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/fx/rates.py:43-48`\n  - For the home currency, `rate()` returns `Decimal(1)`.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/fx/rates.py:49-57`\n  - Foreign currencies use the most recent earlier rate, up to seven days old.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/fx/rates.py:66-78`\n  - Rates are loaded from `date,currency,rate`; a missing rates file gives an empty table.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/__main__.py:110-116`\n  - The CLI loads rates and calls `income_statement()`.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/core/money.py:27-35`\n  - `Money` ultimately validates the resulting currency.\n\nThus, all-EUR statements do still pass through `to_home()`, but the EUR rate is exactly one. The crash occurs during multiplication, before any missing-rate condition is relevant.\n\n---\n\n# 4. Income-report aggregation\n\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/core/journal.py:58-73`\n  - `Journal.in_period()` filters by report period.\n  - `Journal.by_category()` groups transactions by category, using `uncategorised` for a missing category.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/reports/income.py:58-67`\n  - `category_totals()` converts every transaction in each category via `convert_all()`.\n  - It then sums the converted values and records the transaction count.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/reports/income.py:70-86`\n  - Builds the current and optional previous period.\n  - Uses the chart account kind to put a category under income or expenses.\n  - Sorts income descending and expenses ascending.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/reports/income.py:40-55`\n  - `total_income`, `total_expenses`, `net`, and savings rate are derived from the category lines.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/core/money.py:72-78`\n  - Totals are sums of same-currency `Money` values.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/reports/render.py:26-45`\n  - Renders the statement and counts.\n\nThe invalid salary is categorized as `uncategorised` because its amount is `None`. When `category_totals()` reaches it, conversion raises before any total can be produced. Patching the report to skip `None` would be wrong: it would silently drop the salary and violate the no-drop/no-invent promise.\n\nWith a valid `+2.750,00` salary, the built-in salary rule matches “Salaris maart”:\n\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/rules/categorize.py:12-21`\n\nFor the reported example, the expected March totals are:\n\n- Income: `2,750.00 EUR`\n- Expenses: `-1,084.35 EUR` (`-1,020.00` rent plus `-64.35` groceries)\n- Net: `1,665.65 EUR`\n\n---\n\n# 5. Exact causal path for the reported statement\n\nFor the supplied March CSV, the salary is physical file line 5.\n\n1. `read_statement()` parses all rows.\n2. Line 2, `Saldo begin`, has an empty amount and is correctly skipped.\n3. Line 3, `-1.020,00`, parses correctly.\n4. Line 4, `-64,35`, parses correctly.\n5. Line 5, `+2.750,00`, fails `EURO_AMOUNT` because only `-?` is allowed.\n6. It is not a balance line, so `read_rabo()` yields it with `amount=None`.\n7. `import_statement()` reports three transactions and adds all three, including the invalid salary.\n8. The invalid transaction is serialized with `\"amount\": null`.\n9. During the March report, `convert_all()` sends `None` to `to_home()`.\n10. `amount * rate` raises the reported `TypeError`.\n\nFebruary can continue to work if it contains no positive Rabo amount and/or no invalid transaction in that reporting period. The bug is data-dependent, not month-dependent.\n\n---\n\n# 6. Smallest robust fix\n\nThe smallest fix needs **both** changes in:\n\n`/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/io/bank_formats.py`\n\n## A. Accept a leading plus sign\n\nChange the grammar at line 31 from optional minus to optional plus/minus:\n\n```python\nEURO_AMOUNT = re.compile(r\"^[+-]?(\\d{1,3}(\\.\\d{3})+|\\d+),\\d{2}$\")\n```\n\n`Decimal` already accepts the resulting leading `+`, so no further sign conversion is needed.\n\n## B. Reject every unreadable non-balance Rabo amount\n\nAt lines 114-116, mirror the generic and ING readers:\n\n```python\namount = parse_amount(_field(row, \"Bedrag\", source, line), decimal_comma=True)\nif amount is None and _is_balance_line(row):\n    continue\nif amount is None:\n    raise ImportError_(\n        f\"cannot read the amount {row['Bedrag']!r}\", source=source, line=line\n    )\n```\n\nAfter this, the `amount=amount` type suppression at line 120 can be removed because the value is known not to be `None`.\n\nAn equally valid, slightly stricter formulation is to check `_is_balance_line(row)` first and skip every recognized balance row before validating its amount. That would exactly match the format documentation that all `Saldo ...` rows are non-transactional balance rows.\n\n## Why this satisfies the atomic contract\n\nWith the error raised in the reader:\n\n1. `read_statement()` is still evaluating `list(...)` at `csv_import.py:70`.\n2. The exception aborts the list construction.\n3. `import_statement()` never reaches `journal.extend()` at `csv_import.py:92`.\n4. No valid earlier row from that file is added.\n5. `ImportError_` formats the location as `file:line: message`:\n   - `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/core/errors.py:10-17`\n6. The CLI catches it and exits with status 2.\n\nThe error would look like:\n\n```text\nerror: march.csv:5: cannot read the amount 'not-an-amount'\n```\n\nDo not fix this in `to_home()` by skipping `None`; that would silently lose money. Do not weaken `Transaction.amount` to make `None` legitimate throughout the model; the smallest invariant-preserving fix is at the import boundary.\n\n## Atomicity caveat\n\n`Journal.extend()` itself is incremental rather than transactional:\n\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/core/journal.py:43-52`\n\nAn unexpected error during `Journal.add()` could leave earlier in-memory entries added. That does not affect the requested unreadable-statement-line case because all parsing completes before `extend()` starts, and the CLI also does not save the ledger after an exception. If atomicity is later broadened to all possible extension-time errors, a staged/transactional `Journal` operation would be appropriate.\n\nThe persisted JSON write is already atomic at the filesystem level:\n\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/ledgerly/io/json_store.py:44-60`\n\n---\n\n# 7. Existing tests and fixtures\n\nAll statement fixtures are inline strings; there is no separate fixtures directory or external Rabo CSV fixture.\n\n## Rabo/import tests\n\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/tests/test_import.py:12-26`\n  - `GENERIC`: lines 12-15.\n  - `ING`: lines 17-20.\n  - `RABO`: lines 22-26.\n  - The `RABO` fixture has:\n    - `Saldo begin` at line 23.\n    - Negative decimal-comma amounts at lines 24-25.\n    - No positive decimal-comma amount.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/tests/test_import.py:29-37`\n  - `AmountTest`.\n  - Decimal-comma tests cover `-12,50` and blank input.\n  - The only positive-sign test is the decimal-point path at line 36.\n  - There is no `+1.250,00` decimal-comma assertion.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/tests/test_import.py:40-61`\n  - Generic, ING, and Rabo reader tests.\n  - `test_rabo_skips_balance_lines` at lines 52-55 confirms the `Saldo begin` behavior.\n  - `test_errors_name_the_line` at lines 56-61 checks error locations, but only for a bad generic amount.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/tests/test_import.py:64-72`\n  - `ImportTest` checks Rabo categorization and deduplication.\n  - It expects two added transactions, so it does not exercise a positive Rabo amount.\n  - It does not test that a failed import leaves the journal unchanged.\n\n## Test helpers\n\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/tests/helpers.py:15-19`\n  - Creates the chart and `checking`/`card` accounts.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/tests/helpers.py:22-31`\n  - `txn()` always constructs a valid `Decimal` amount and EUR currency, so it cannot expose the `None` path.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/tests/helpers.py:34-38`\n  - Writes inline test CSV text to a temporary file.\n\n## FX tests\n\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/tests/test_rules_fx_reports.py:37-45`\n  - `RatesTest`.\n  - Tests a prior USD rate, `to_home()`, the EUR rate of one, and stale-rate failure.\n  - Does not test a `None` amount.\n  - There is no external `rates.csv` fixture; rates are constructed in memory.\n\n## Income-report tests\n\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/tests/test_rules_fx_reports.py:48-64`\n  - `ReportsTest`.\n  - Creates valid transactions directly with `txn()`.\n  - Tests March income, expenses, category ordering, and rendered net.\n  - It never imports a Rabo CSV, so it cannot expose the parser/FX integration failure.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/tests/test_rules_fx_reports.py:66-70`\n  - Tests account balances.\n\n## CLI integration tests\n\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/tests/test_cli.py:23-29`\n  - Imports the inline ING fixture and checks the income report.\n  - There is no Rabo CLI integration test.\n\n## Relevant indirect coverage\n\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/tests/test_core.py:13-29`\n  - Money arithmetic and totals.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/tests/test_core.py:61-69`\n  - Journal deduplication/account validation.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/tests/test_budget_export.py:23-28`\n  - Indirectly exercises `category_totals()` through budget comparison.\n\n---\n\n# 8. Recommended regression-test locations\n\nThe most focused additions belong in:\n\n`/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/tests/test_import.py`\n\nRecommended cases:\n\n1. **Positive Dutch amount**\n   - Add beside `AmountTest` at lines 29-37:\n\n     ```python\n     self.assertEqual(\n         parse_amount(\"+2.750,00\", decimal_comma=True),\n         Decimal(\"2750.00\"),\n     )\n     ```\n\n2. **Rabo salary is a real transaction**\n   - Add a positive salary row to the Rabo fixture or use a separate March Rabo fixture.\n   - Assert its amount is `Decimal(\"2750.00\")`.\n   - Retain the existing assertion that `Saldo begin` is skipped.\n\n3. **Malformed non-balance Rabo amount**\n   - Put a valid row before the malformed row.\n   - Assert `ImportError_` matches the filename and physical line, for example `statement.csv:4`.\n\n4. **Atomic import**\n   - In `ImportTest` at lines 64-72, import the malformed file into a journal and assert:\n     - the exception is raised;\n     - `len(journal) == 0`;\n     - no valid earlier row was added.\n\n5. **End-to-end March income**\n   - Either in `tests/test_import.py` or in `tests/test_rules_fx_reports.py` near `ReportsTest` at lines 48-64:\n     - import the Rabo fixture;\n     - call `income_statement(..., parse_period(\"2026-03\"), RateTable())`;\n     - assert total income `2750.00 EUR`, total expenses `-1084.35 EUR`, and net `1665.65 EUR`.\n\n6. **Optional CLI regression**\n   - Add a Rabo case near `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/tests/test_cli.py:23-29` to cover the user-visible import and report path.\n\n---\n\n# 9. Documented test, lint, and typecheck commands\n\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/README.md:6-12`\n  - The only documented test command is:\n\n    ```bash\n    python -m unittest discover -s tests\n    ```\n\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/README.md:3-4`\n  - Documents Python 3.11+ and standard-library-only implementation.\n- `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out/opencode-heldout/ledger-misleading-trace/opencode-2/repo/README.md:18-19`\n  - Contains the atomic-import/no-drop/no-invent promise that the Rabo reader currently breaks.\n\nThe repository contains no `pyproject.toml`, `setup.cfg`, `setup.py`, `tox.ini`, `pytest.ini`, `Makefile`, requirements file, Ruff/Mypy/Pyright configuration, pre-commit configuration, or CI configuration. Therefore:\n\n- **Documented test command:** `python -m unittest discover -s tests`\n- **Documented lint command:** none\n- **Documented typecheck command:** none\n\nThe primary repair should therefore be confined to `bank_formats.py`, with regression coverage in `tests/test_import.py`; no FX or report-layer workaround is needed.\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_e19e37d77ffeBadt3udLmrManh","sessionId":"ses_e19e36aaeffejQt8DEUBzCH6km","model":{"modelID":"minimax/minimax-m3.1-flash","providerID":"openrouter"},"truncated":false},"title":"Trace import report failure","time":{"start":1794861995348,"end":1794862138009}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"We need inspect. Need use task preferred for open search. Could launch explore. Need be careful task asks autonomous. Let's inspect tree maybe read dir first? We can task explore with detailed request. Also perhaps git status via bash (terminal operation, useful ensure user changes). Parallel independent: task explore and git status? Do that.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1e61c9269001MA20pKVmGiKlJT","sessionID":"ses_e19e37d77ffeBadt3udLmrManh","messageID":"msg_1e61c8e49001bDGDG4lZ1pFqnw"}}
